#X text 545 439 eof;
#X obj 600 438 print error;
#X text 20 540 A bare symbol opens the file too \, which is why [openpanel]
goes straight in above. Sending open and run 1 together in one message
is fine: the stream fills up before it plays \, and that is not a dropout.;
#X text 20 604 speed resamples rather than repitching separately: at
speed 2 the file plays twice as fast and an octave higher \, which is
what a file player usually means. Negative speed is not supported in
this version.;
#X text 20 668 A file whose sample rate differs from Pd's is resampled
to Pd's rate \, and speed multiplies that ratio. Opening a second file
replaces the first and stops playback \; a seek past the end clamps
there and reads as end of file. Errors carry a short reason: nofile
\, format \, noopen \, seek or underflow.;
